WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.989
In the morning at the station, a quick coffee to go: for many people that is part of everyday life. The problem is the cup. It is used for only a few minutes and then ends up in the bin. In Germany, billions of these disposable cups are thrown away every year.

00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:49.708
Since 2023, larger restaurants, cafés and snack bars in Germany have had to offer reusable packaging for takeaway food and drinks as well. Small businesses with few staff and little floor space are exempt, but they must fill containers that customers bring. The reusable cup may not cost more than the disposable one. Often you pay a deposit of one or two euros and get it back when you return the cup.

00:00:49.958 --> 00:01:10.924
Has the law achieved anything? The results are mixed. Many cafés offer reusable cups, but only a few customers use them. Some find it impractical to carry a cup around. Others don't even know the option exists, because it is not explained clearly enough.

00:01:11.174 --> 00:01:31.527
Some cities are therefore going a step further. They have introduced a shared system: you can buy the cup in one café and return it in another. Environmental groups say the best solution is still the simplest — take five minutes and drink your coffee in the café.
